      {
        "id": "531046",
        "date_added": "2026-11-22 11:34:36",
        "twitter_handle": null,
        "display_name": null,
        "comment": "FluxEngine client build 1.0.3.113 (Delphi PE32, compiled 2026-11-21 18:17:00 UTC). Plaintext of d3dx9_43.bin served by hxxps://remoto.painelst[.]com/api/source-file.php on 2026-11-22 10:54 UTC, decrypted with the dhlib master key (the panel re-encrypts per download, so container hashes are useless). Same strings, token and protocol as build 1.0.3.111 (c424a715). C2 IP from Cloudflare-API TXT ip.\u003czone\u003e; TCP 9000 control / 9002 video; the panel host 72.167.150[.]114 had TCP 9000/9002 open on 2026-11-22 (current TXT value not read).\n\nChain (static analysis): DOC-*.vbs -\u003e regsvr32 /i:%TEMP%\\t\u003cdigits\u003e.sct scrobj.dll (recon scriptlet) -\u003e installer scriptlet -\u003e C:\\\u003c8 letters\u003e\\ with signed AutoIt3 (renamed) + compiled script -\u003e in-memory dhlib.dll (InitModule) -\u003e AES container from the operator panel -\u003e hollowed attrib.exe -\u003e FluxEngine client. C2 address is read from a DNS TXT record through the Cloudflare API with an embedded token.\nRules, IOCs: https://github.com/harperjohnsai/detections/tree/main/iocs/2026-11-fluxengine\nHarper Johns, security researcher\nMore research: youtube.com/@HarperJohnsAI"
      }
    ],
